ics building with a commemorative outdoor bust.","evidence_claim":"K-State reports that Martin Luther King Jr. gave his final university speech at Ahearn Field House in 1968 and that a memorial bust was installed outside in 2007.","source_url":"https://www.k-state.edu/maps/buildings/AFH/","source_title":"Ahearn Field House | K-State campus map","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Treat this as an exterior landmark stop; facility access varies with athletics and events.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"kstate-peters-rec-complex","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Chester E. Peters Recreation Complex","title":"Check out the Rec Complex","subtitle":"Saturday afternoon · 1831 Olympic Dr.","notes":"Tour the public-facing complex with a friend and ask the desk about current eligibility and entry rules before planning a workout or court time.","short_summary":"A large campus recreation facility with courts, tracks, climbing, and fitness areas.","evidence_claim":"K-State Recreational Services lists courts, climbing and bouldering areas, indoor tracks, fitness areas, and accessible features at the Peters Recreation Complex.","source_url":"https://recservices.k-state.edu/complex/","source_title":"Peters Recreation Complex | K-State Recreational Services","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Entry eligibility, guest access, and activity availability are not specified on this facility overview; verify with Recreational Services.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"kstate-mccain-auditorium","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"McCain Auditorium","title":"End with a look at McCain’s calendar","subtitle":"Saturday evening · 1501 Goldstein Circle","notes":"Check the performance calendar and choose an age-appropriate future program. Confirm ticketing and event details directly before making plans.","short_summary":"K-State’s live-performing-arts venue and Music Department home.","evidence_claim":"K-State identifies McCain Auditorium as the campus cultural center for live performing arts and notes that it serves students and the general public.","source_url":"https://mccain.k-state.edu/about/","source_title":"About McCain Auditorium | Kansas State University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Individual performances can have separate ticketing and schedules; consult the official event listing before attending.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
